{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"40659144c078fae3396368780526451b8c97500ffc92fc5b42a0d6e66c449941","digest":{"component_or_area":"push.py lock-artifact exclusion and failure coverage","key_entities":["_ignore_lock_artifacts","src/rebar/_store/push.py","info/exclude","tests/unit/test_commit_and_push_tickets_branch_heldout.py",".ticket-write.lock","O_APPEND","os.write","PushDeliveryError","stage-failed"],"problem_keywords":["lock artifact exclusion","metadata corruption","concurrent access","atomicity","test coverage","failure handling"],"propositions":["Concurrent buffered appends to info/exclude can interleave and corrupt patterns at the byte level, silently disabling lock-artifact exclusion.","The exclusion-write failure path (push.py:651-655) and git-status failure path (push.py:673-678) lack direct test coverage in the held-out suite.","Lock artifacts can be committed to the tree if exclusion metadata is not present or corrupted before git add -A runs.","Replacing buffered two-write append with atomic POSIX O_APPEND write eliminates byte-level corruption; whole-line duplication remains possible and is acceptable."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787723356997645001,"uuid":"794751a6-ef86-454f-a38f-8b258d2e6a84"}